 PROBLEM STATEMENT

  Hospitals need an organized way to maintain patient information and manage the order in
which patients wait for consultation. Manual record keeping can make it difficult to search
for a patient's details, update or remove records, and keep track of the consultation queue.
Therefore, a Hospital Patient Data Management System is to be developed in C++ using a
Doubly Linked List and a Queue. The system must store each patient's unique ID, name,
age, contact details, and reason for visiting. The Doubly Linked List should support
inserting new patient records, displaying all stored records, searching by patient ID,
updating details, and deleting a record when required. Each linked-list node should contain
pointers to both the previous and next nodes, enabling traversal in either direction. A
separate Queue should manage patients waiting for consultation. When a patient joins the
queue, their ID or reference should be added at the rear; when the doctor is ready, the
patient at the front should be called first and removed from the waiting queue, following the
First In, First Out (FIFO) rule. The program should provide a clear menu for performing
these operations and display suitable messages when a patient is not found or the queue
is empty. The system should keep patient-record operations separate from queue
operations so that removing someone from the waiting queue does not automatically
delete their stored patient record. 
